252 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 96 0 R
/E (This gap persists despite the fact that physical gold has generated yield for institutional participants for decades, through an established, low-complexity mechanism largely inaccessible to individual holders: short-term, collateralized gold financing. Bullion banks, refiners, and jewelers routinely borrow physical gold as working capital, paying a lease rate for the privilege, a practice as old as institutional gold markets themselves. This yield source is real, understood, and structurally simple, but it has remained the province of large financial institutions with direct relationships to bullion markets, entirely outside the reach of a typical token holder.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
253 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 96 0 R
/E (Syncrate addresses both halves of this problem through two distinct, purpose-built instruments rather than a single blended product. XAUs gives holders pure, fully-reserved exposure to the value of physical gold, with no yield, no counterparty exposure, and no compromise to the underlying reserve. syXAUs gives XAUs holders an explicit, optional path to deploy that value into the same gold-backed financing arrangements institutions have relied on for decades, with yield accruing transparently onchain. A holder is never forced into this exposure; they choose it, deliberately, understanding that it introduces real counterparty risk in exchange for real, asset-backed yield.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
254 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 96 0 R
/E (This separation is the core design principle underlying Syncrate. Where existing gold tokens force a single, undifferentiated risk profile onto every holder, Syncrate allows the decision to seek yield, and the risk that comes with it, to remain entirely with the individual holder, not embedded silently in the base asset.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
